  "bases_notes": "One row per embedded field or embedded interface element, because embedding is the only inheritance Go has: `type Options struct { Shape }` gives Options everything Shape has, kind `base`; `type Repo interface { Bucket }` is a contract composed of contracts, kind `interface`. Method sets are not bases — `Shape.Area` is a member of Shape, not a supertype of anything. Go has no `extends` anywhere, so no row here is a `trait`.",
  "synthetic_notes": "`init_linux.go` and `init_other.go` only. Both declare `metrics.Init` and exactly one of them is compiled, which is decided by a `//go:build` line the parser can read and cannot evaluate: a parser does not run the build. So the file's own declaration list is not the package's declaration list, which is a cannot-enumerate state rather than a duplicate definition. No other Go file earns a mark: a second file in the same directory is not a second copy of anything, and `doc.go` declaring nothing is a real answer."
